@startuml
' Deployment diagram for running the project without Docker
' Project: shelter_project2 / PawCare

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam componentStyle uml2
left to right direction

node "User Device" as client {
  artifact "Browser" as browser
}

node "Host PC / Server" as host {
  node "Python environment\n(.venv)" as pyenv {
    artifact "Django app\nmanage.py runserver\nor run_https_server.py" as django
  }

  node "Local PostgreSQL" as pgnode {
    database "PostgreSQL\n(shelter_db)" as db
  }

  folder "media/" as media
  folder "staticfiles/" as staticfiles
}

cloud "External services" as ext {
  component "SMTP server" as smtp
}

browser --> django : HTTP / HTTPS
django --> db : SQL
django --> media : file upload / read
django --> staticfiles : static assets
django --> smtp : email reminders

note right of django
  The project can be started locally with:
  - python manage.py runserver
  - or scripts/run_https.ps1 + run_https_server.py

  PostgreSQL must be installed separately.
  media/ and staticfiles/ are regular folders on disk.
end note

@enduml